a9y18qlte: Chlorophyll on iOS 16: device registration without MTLCopyAllDevices, CA probe fixes

iOS 16's Metal.framework exports MTLAddDevice and MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice but not MTLCopyAllDevices
(dlsym NULL: bgmtl_adddev crashed calling it, the CARenderer probe and the injection refused to register).
MTLAddDevice asserts `_deviceArray != NULL`; on iOS 16 MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice's dispatch_once makes that
array and the queue MTLAddDevice syncs on before it enumerates (Metal 0x181a34050 in 20H392's cache), and it
answers the array's only device. src/a9y_devices.h lists devices through it when MTLCopyAllDevices is missing;
the injection, bgmtl_adddev and bgmtl_carenderer_probe use it, and the injection logs whether the default device
is ours after registering.

bgmtl_ca_probe read [cb status] right after commit (asynchronous now: every function was "failed", in an unflushed
file); it waits, writes line by line, and with BG_CA_HASH prints a hash and the first pixel instead of 8 KB of hex.

Assisted-by: LLM

